{{Elections in Arkansas}}
The '''1992 United States Senate election in Arkansas''' was held on November 3, 1992. Incumbent Democratic Senator [[Dale Bumpers]] won re-election to a fourth term. His Republican opponent was future Arkansas lieutenant governor, governor, and two-time presidential candidate [[Mike Huckabee]], a church pastor from [[Texarkana, Arkansas|Texarkana]].

The 1992 election coincided with the [[1992 United States presidential election in Arkansas|1992 presidential election]], in which Arkansas governor [[Bill Clinton]], who was elected as [[President of the United States]], won his home state. While Bumpers had previously won his home state with over 60% of the vote, Clinton secured only 53.21% of the vote. Bumpers served another term in the Senate before retiring in 1998.

